---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ReleaseNotes from '../../components/ReleaseNotes.astro';
import releases from '../../data/fieldade-releases.json';
const latest = releases[0];
---
<Base title="FieldADE" description="FieldADE is the iPhone app for HomeADE, the desk on your computer where your agents work. File what comes in under a project with one swipe, and start a chat that already knows the project. A change waits until you allow it." image="/work/fieldade.png">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={11} eyebrow="iPhone app" title="FieldADE">
    <p class="lede">FieldADE is the iPhone app for <a href="/homeade">HomeADE</a>, the desk on your computer where your agents work. From the phone you see what is due, file what just came in, and start a chat that already knows the project. A change waits until you allow it.</p>
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/fieldade/setup">Setup guide</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://jtembry.github.io/embry-wiki/fieldade/">Wiki</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/homeade">HomeADE, the desktop app</a>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section product">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="product-shots">
        <img class="shot look-pro-only" src="/work/fieldade.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE on an iPhone: a chat with Claude, with a card asking to allow or deny a file edit" width="460" height="1000" />
        <img class="shot look-dos-only" src="/work/fieldade-dos.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE on an iPhone: a chat with Claude, with a card asking to allow or deny a file edit, in the DOS look" width="460" height="1000" />
        <img class="shot look-pro-only" src="/work/fieldade-list.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE's Sessions screen: how much of each assistant's limit is used, and the list of open chats" width="460" height="1000" />
        <img class="shot look-dos-only" src="/work/fieldade-list-dos.png?v=20261120" alt="FieldADE's Sessions screen: how much of each assistant's limit is used, and the list of open chats, in the DOS look" width="460" height="1000" />
      </div>

      <p class="card-actions"><a class="store-badge" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/fieldade/id6828288883" rel="noopener"><img src="/brand/app-store-badge.svg" alt="Download on the App Store" width="132" height="44" /></a></p>
      <p class="fine">Version {latest.version} &middot; iOS 17 or later &middot; <a href="/fieldade/setup">Setup guide</a> &middot; <a href="/fieldade/privacy">Privacy policy</a></p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>Something comes in on the phone: a mail, a text, a photo, a link. You file it under a project with one swipe. The note lands in the same folder your agents read on the computer. The next chat on that project opens knowing it. File from the phone or from the desk, it is one folder, so nothing is explained twice.</p>

      <h2>Ingest from wherever the work shows up</h2>
      <p>Mail and texts arrive in the app. Swipe to file an item under the right project, archive it, delete it, or draft a reply. You send the reply. Share a photo, a file, or a link into FieldADE and it lands in Ingest, the inbox of the notes. Point the camera at a business card and add the contact from the scan. <a href="/map">The sample screens</a> show the same three steps: something comes in, one swipe shows the plan, and the note shows up on the project.</p>

      <h2>The notes are the memory</h2>
      <p>Projects and areas are the second brain: plain notes in a folder you own. Open one in the app and read the brief before you start a chat. The agent reads that same folder, so its answer starts from the record, and you can check it against the note. Every item you file makes the next chat better informed, so the folder is worth more each month. You are not retyping the context into a fresh session, and you are not trusting a hidden memory inside a chat app.</p>

      <h2>The board, not a single chat</h2>
      <p>Open the phone and you get the queue. Today shows what is due and what is waiting. The Agents screen lists the open chats, the model on each one, and how much of that assistant's limit is used. A follow-up an agent schedules shows on Today and on the calendar. You filter, rename, and search chats, including closed ones, so a decision has a place to live after the chat ends. On iOS 26 or later, a widget can sit on the home screen.</p>

      <h2>Skills and models you can inspect</h2>
      <p>A skill is a written set of steps an agent can follow. Before you hand a chat more work, you can see which of Claude, Codex, and Grok are installed, and the skills, rules, and hooks on that machine, so you know what the agent can do and what it will follow. You pick the model for the chat. A file edit or a command waits until you allow it or deny it.</p>

      <h2>Your data stays in the folder you chose</h2>
      <p>There is no FieldADE account. Notes stay in that folder. The note reader will not open a note marked private. A chat sends its prompt to the model under your own login, and only when you run it. The <a href="/fieldade/privacy">privacy policy</a> says what leaves the devices. The agents themselves run in <a href="/homeade">HomeADE</a> on your computer. FieldADE is how you reach that desk from the phone.</p>

      <h2>The phone by itself</h2>
      <p>FieldADE can also run with no desktop app. Turn on Phone only, pick a notes folder on the phone, and enter an Anthropic API key. Chats then run on the phone and bill that key. To look around first, tap Try the sample vault on the Today screen. The <a href="/fieldade/setup#no-mac">setup guide</a> has the steps.</p>

      <h2 id="releases">Release notes</h2>
      <p>What changed in each version. The newest is the text on the App Store under What's New.</p>
      <ReleaseNotes releases={releases} />

      <p class="back"><a href="/products">All products</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .product h2 { scroll-margin-top: 6.5rem; }
  .product-shots { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: .75rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .shot { display: block; flex: 1 1 0; min-width: 0; max-width: 220px; height: auto; border-radius: 22px; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .card-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: .6rem; margin: .5rem 0; }
  .store-badge { display: inline-flex; line-height: 0; }
  .store-badge img { height: 44px; width: auto; }
  .fine { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; }
</style>
